{"abstract":"Drawing on ethnographic fieldwork among Ghanaian officials and international developers in the field of health information systems, we investigate how innovations in health data infrastructures are aligned with global practices of epidemiological accountability. The digital health information system DHIS2 has been adopted in various low- and middle-income countries, including Ghana. While global stakeholders render public health a matter of efficiency and accountability, public health professionals attune at various levels to emerging global health priorities and data practices, e.g. the translation of standard case definitions and quantitative measures into local contexts, or innovations in reporting channels of key public health indicators.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Thiel, Alena","Christensen, Lars Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-830017"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"attuning to global health health data infrastructuring epidemiological accountability and digital labor in ghana","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01459740.2025.2535990","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-830017","identifier":[{"id":"105013803487","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-da8b3566-057f-48f5-bfc9-b90f63106d6c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-23167DA53E0A7517F7FECB924BE4DEFD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/01459740.2025.2535990","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Theology, Centre for African Studies - Technical area, Centre for African Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Alena","key":"thielpau","last":"Thiel","locid":"8eaf409f-f6a1-439e-a8e1-c7c1da0c88da","name":"Thiel, Alena","orcid":"0000-0002-1092-1140","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/01459740.2025.2535990","issn":["01459740","15455882"],"issn_org":["01459740"],"journal":"Medical Anthropology","pages":"1","status":"p","title":"Medical Anthropology","title_org":"Medical Anthropology: Cross Cultural Studies in Health and Illness"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105013803487"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-da8b3566-057f-48f5-bfc9-b90f63106d6c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Attuning to Global Health: Health Data Infrastructuring, Epidemiological Accountability and Digital Labor in Ghana","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-830017","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The widespread pain and muscular fatigue characteristics of fibromyalgia are believed to be mediated by central mechanisms. Low-dose naltrexone (LDN) has emerged as a new treatment option for fibromyalgia, possibly modulating central mechanisms via glial or opioid receptors. METHODS: In the randomized, placebo-controlled FINAL trial, 99 women with fibromyalgia were treated with LDN or placebo for 12 weeks. In this secondary analysis, we examined the potential effects of LDN versus placebo on changes from baseline in pain tolerance, temporal summation of pain, and conditioned pain modulation (CPM) in the complete case population (45 versus 47 participants). Measures of muscular fatigue were evaluated using the 30-s chair stand test and a shoulder abduction test. RESULTS: Of the five examined outcomes, only change in CPM showed a significant between-group difference with greater enhancement following LDN treatment (2.0 kPa; 95% confidence interval (CI) 0.4-3.7 kPa) compared with placebo. Within-group changes in CPM showed an increase of 1.2 kPa (95% CI 0.05-2.4 kPa) in the LDN group and a possible decrease of 0.8 kPa (95% CI - 1.9 to 0.4 kPa) in the placebo group. CONCLUSIONS: We found a significant between-group difference in CPM change in favor of LDN. However, this difference was partly explained by a decrease in CPM in the placebo group. Sensitivity analyses showed no association between changes in CPM and clinical pain improvement, suggesting that the group-difference in CPM is a random finding. STUDY REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov (NCT0427877; registered on 30 January 2020).","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bruun, Karin Due","Christensen, Robin","Amris, Kirstine","Blichfeldt-Eckhardt, Morten Rune","Bye-Møller, Lars","Henriksen, Marius","Alkjær, Tine","Toft, Palle","Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","Vaegter, Henrik Bjarke"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-814075"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Bruun, Karin Due"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of naltrexone on spinal and supraspinal pain mechanisms and functional capacity in women with fibromyalgia exploratory outcomes from the randomized placebo controlled final trial","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s40263-025-01183-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-814075","identifier":[{"id":"PMC12165890","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"105002301638","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40214857","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a71d2912-a0bc-4d10-aaf7-363bae60cfa9","sdu-bc2e13f3-ac9b-42b7-b7fa-12720fec1d30"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-48BE19EE4891D5A263168D1EB9A8EE6E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s40263-025-01183-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/454301113/s40263-025-01183-7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/291173761/s40263-025-01183-7.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Exercise and Muscle"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin Due","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","locid":"e276834f-a612-4fb4-9c69-87830182729d","name":"Bruun, Karin Due","orcid":"0000-0002-3106-2461","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"04bf2bf9-a6d8-4be8-93fd-82f3f2ddc9ba","name":"Christensen, Robin","orcid":"0000-0002-6600-0631","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kirstine","key":"amrispau","last":"Amris","name":"Amris, Kirstine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Rune","key":"blichfeldteckhardtpau","last":"Blichfeldt-Eckhardt","locid":"f603c66f-99ca-4f58-984c-8a37cd15773c","name":"Blichfeldt-Eckhardt, Morten Rune","orcid":"0000-0002-7759-5642","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Lars","key":"byemøllerpau","last":"Bye-Møller","name":"Bye-Møller, Lars","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marius","key":"henriksenpau","last":"Henriksen","name":"Henriksen, Marius","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 4","first":"Tine","key":"alkjaerpau","last":"Alkjaer","locid":"d0ff1f22-b755-48d5-b5c9-94a9ef4367ac","name":"Alkjær, Tine","name_org":"Alkjaer, Tine","orcid":"0000-0002-9105-3882","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Palle","key":"toftpau","last":"Toft","locid":"a06bd771-b511-4783-8c06-333267c94154","name":"Toft, Palle","orcid":"0000-0002-3188-449X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"holsgaardlarsenpau","last":"Holsgaard-Larsen","locid":"3c1cf5a4-81b1-49f3-ad79-d086b74b1561","name":"Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4106-6930","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Bjarke","key":"vaegterpau","last":"Vaegter","locid":"b35dd901-cb2f-4f50-a2c5-65e1a4752f02","name":"Vægter, Henrik Bjarke","name_org":"Vaegter, Henrik Bjarke","orcid":"0000-0002-7707-9947","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40214857"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s40263-025-01183-7","issn":["11727047","11791934"],"issn_org":["11727047"],"issue":"7","journal":"CNS Drugs","pages":"685-692","publisher":"Adis","status":"p","title":"CNS Drugs","volume":"39"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105002301638"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a71d2912-a0bc-4d10-aaf7-363bae60cfa9","sdu-bc2e13f3-ac9b-42b7-b7fa-12720fec1d30"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effect of Naltrexone on Spinal and Supraspinal Pain Mechanisms and Functional Capacity in Women with Fibromyalgia : Exploratory Outcomes from the Randomized Placebo-Controlled FINAL Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-814075","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Low-dose naltrexone is used to treat fibromyalgia despite minimal evidence for its efficacy. This trial aimed to investigate whether 12-week treatment with 6 mg low-dose naltrexone was superior to placebo for reducing pain in women with fibromyalgia. Methods: We did a single-centre, randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial in Denmark. We enrolled women aged 18–64 years who were diagnosed with fibromyalgia. Participants were randomly assigned 1:1 to receive low-dose naltrexone (6 mg) or an identical-appearing placebo, using a computerised algorithm with no stratifications applied. Participants, investigators, outcome assessors, and statistical analysts were all masked to treatment allocation. The primary outcome was change in pain intensity on an 11-point numeric rating scale from baseline to week 12, in the intention-to-treat population. Safety was assessed in participants in the intention-to-treat population who received at least one dose of their allocated intervention. This trial was registered with ClincalTrials.gov (NCT04270877) and EudraCT (2019-000702-30). Findings: We screened 158 participants for eligibility from Jan 6, 2021, to Dec 27, 2022, and 99 patients were randomly assigned to low-dose naltrexone (n=49) or placebo (n=50). The mean age was 50·6 years (SD 8·8), one (1%) of 99 participants was Arctic Asian and 98 (99%) were White. No participants were lost to follow-up. The mean change in pain intensity was –1·3 points (95% CI –1·7 to –0·8) in the low-dose naltrexone group and –0·9 (–1·4 to –0·5) in the placebo group, corresponding to a between-group difference of –0·34 (–0·95 to 0·27; p=0·27, Cohen's d 0·23). Discontinuations due to adverse events were four (8%) of 49 in the low-dose naltrexone group and three (6%) of 50 in the placebo group. 41 (84%) of 49 patients in the low-dose naltrexone group had an adverse event versus 43 (86%) of 50 in the placebo group. One serious adverse event occurred in the placebo group and no deaths occurred. Interpretation: This study did not show that treatment with low-dose naltrexone was superior to placebo in relieving pain. Our results indicate that low-dose naltrexone might improve memory problems associated with fibromyalgia, and we suggest that future trials investigate this further. Funding: The Danish Rheumatism Association, Odense University Hospital, Danielsen's Foundation, and the Oak Foundation.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Bruun, Karin Due","Christensen, Robin","Amris, Kirstine","Vægter, Henrik Bjarke","Blichfeldt-Eckhardt, Morten Rune","Bye-Møller, Lars","Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","Toft, Palle"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-713863"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Bruun, Karin Due"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"naltrexone 000000000006 mg once daily versus placebo in women with fibromyalgia a randomised double blind placebo controlled trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85179027222","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Study data were collected and managed using REDCap electronic data capture tools hosted at OPEN, Open Patient Data Explorative Network, Odense University Hospital, Region of Southern Denmark. Thanks to Claire Gudex, Department of Clinical Research, University of Southern Denmark, for commenting on and editing the manuscript. Operating expenses were covered by funding from the Danish Rheumatism Association (A6158), Odense University Hospital's PhD fund for operating expenses (A3650), and Aase og Ejnar Danielsen's Foundation. The Section for Biostatistics and Evidence-Based Research at the Parker Institute, Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg Hospital is supported by a core grant from the Oak Foundation (OCAY-18-774-OFIL). Study data were collected and managed using REDCap electronic data capture tools hosted at OPEN, Open Patient Data Explorative Network, Odense University Hospital, Region of Southern Denmark. Thanks to Claire Gudex, Department of Clinical Research, University of Southern Denmark, for commenting on and editing the manuscript. Operating expenses were covered by funding from the Danish Rheumatism Association (A6158), Odense University Hospital's PhD fund for operating expenses (A3650), and Aase og Ejnar Danielsen's Foundation. The Section for Biostatistics and Evidence-Based Research at the Parker Institute, Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg Hospital is supported by a core grant from the Oak Foundation (OCAY-18-774-OFIL)."],"id":"S01-000.00-713863","identifier":[{"id":"38258677","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85179027222","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-3d350c45-827a-4900-ada0-a85a81871560"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2649199F738DC61DF115A751D0C68C22"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Patient and family representative, SDU/OUH"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Karin","key":"duebruunpau","last":"Due Bruun","locid":"e276834f-a612-4fb4-9c69-87830182729d","name":"Bruun, Karin Due","name_org":"Due Bruun, Karin","orcid":"0000-0002-3106-2461","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"04bf2bf9-a6d8-4be8-93fd-82f3f2ddc9ba","name":"Christensen, Robin","orcid":"0000-0002-6600-0631","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirstine","key":"amrispau","last":"Amris","name":"Amris, Kirstine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Bjarke","key":"vaegterpau","last":"Vaegter","locid":"b35dd901-cb2f-4f50-a2c5-65e1a4752f02","name":"Vægter, Henrik Bjarke","name_org":"Vaegter, Henrik Bjarke","orcid":"0000-0002-7707-9947","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Rune","key":"blichfeldteckhardtpau","last":"Blichfeldt-Eckhardt","locid":"f603c66f-99ca-4f58-984c-8a37cd15773c","name":"Blichfeldt-Eckhardt, Morten Rune","orcid":"0000-0002-7759-5642","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"byemøllerpau","last":"Bye-Møller","name":"Bye-Møller, Lars","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"holsgaardlarsenpau","last":"Holsgaard-Larsen","locid":"3c1cf5a4-81b1-49f3-ad79-d086b74b1561","name":"Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4106-6930","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Palle","key":"toftpau","last":"Toft","locid":"a06bd771-b511-4783-8c06-333267c94154","name":"Toft, Palle","orcid":"0000-0002-3188-449X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38258677"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s2665-9913(23)00278-3","issn":["26659913"],"issue":"1","journal":"The Lancet Rheumatology","publisher":"Lancet Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Rheumatology","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85179027222"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-3d350c45-827a-4900-ada0-a85a81871560"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Naltrexone 6 mg once daily versus placebo in women with fibromyalgia : a randomised, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-713863","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Participatory Design (PD) aims for inclusivity, but the level of inclusion varies widely. Inclusion often means integrating stakeholder perspectives into design processes, often neglecting bi-directionality, where communities also have agendas. True collaboration rests on mutual understanding, acknowledging the dynamic nature of community collaboration and the holistic impact of shaping relationships. This workshop will explore collaboration challenges and practices with marginalized communities. It will draw on the organisers’ extensive experiences with diverse groups, including nomadic and resettled indigenous communities in Namibia, Rohingya refugees in Bangladesh, and Syrian war refugees in Jordan. The workshop encourages sharing and reflecting on experiences with marginalized communities, welcoming contributions from participants to enrich discussions and enhance collective understanding of collaborative practices.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rodil, Kasper","Kandjengo, Shorty","Maasz, Donovan","Ahsan, Hasib","Christensen, Lars Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776407"],"event":{"acronym":"PDC","title":"Participatory Design Conference"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Namibia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Donkerbos Community","Namibia University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Global South","Marginalised Communities","Participatory Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparative insights for community based co design bi directional inclusive strategies between marginalised communities and researchers in participatory design","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85204902234","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776407","identifier":[{"id":"85204902234","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-663e67b2-4ac5-41f4-b969-439ccdfeb60d"],"keyword":["Global South","Marginalised Communities","Participatory Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-769FFC5266B6C071E7C61CF385DE0167"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"na","key":"donkerbos community","loc":["Namibia","Africa"],"name":"Donkerbos Community","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"na","key":"namibia university of science and technology","loc":["Namibia","Africa"],"name":"Namibia University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"rodilpau","last":"Rodil","name":"Rodil, Kasper","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shorty","key":"kandjengopau","last":"Kandjengo","name":"Kandjengo, Shorty","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Donovan","key":"maaszpau