ed"]},"sid":["itu-9ead329e-331d-4056-9a41-7238df054a8a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Action Research Booklet","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747253","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Participatory Design (PD) aims for inclusivity, but the level of inclusion varies widely. Inclusion often means integrating stakeholder perspectives into design processes, often neglecting bi-directionality, where communities also have agendas. True collaboration rests on mutual understanding, acknowledging the dynamic nature of community collaboration and the holistic impact of shaping relationships. This workshop will explore collaboration challenges and practices with marginalized communities. It will draw on the organisers’ extensive experiences with diverse groups, including nomadic and resettled indigenous communities in Namibia, Rohingya refugees in Bangladesh, and Syrian war refugees in Jordan. The workshop encourages sharing and reflecting on experiences with marginalized communities, welcoming contributions from participants to enrich discussions and enhance collective understanding of collaborative practices.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Rodil, Kasper","Kandjengo, Shorty","Maasz, Donovan","Ahsan, Hasib","Christensen, Lars Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-736429"],"event":{"end":"2024-08-16","place":"Sibu, my","start":"2024-08-12","title":"18th Participatory Design Conference","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Namibia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Donkerbos Community","Namibia University of Science and Technology"],"keyword":["Community based co design","Marginalised Communities","Participatory Design","Workshop"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparative insights for community based co design bi directional inclusive strategies between marginalised communities and researchers in participatory design","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85204902234&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-736429","identifier":[{"id":"85204902234","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-dbfd54b5-466f-4f3c-8768-7a62d27384c7"],"keyword":["Community-based co-design","Participatory Design","Workshop","marginalised communities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-769FFC5266B6C071E7C61CF385DE0167"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Human Machine Interaction","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Section for Media Technology - Campus Aalborg","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Sustainability and Planning, Centre for Sustainable and Digital Transformation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"na","key":"donkerbos community","loc":["Namibia","Africa"],"name":"Donkerbos Community","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"na","key":"namibia university of science and technology","loc":["Namibia","Africa"],"name":"Namibia University of Science and Technology","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kasper","key":"rodilpau","last":"Rodil","locid":"43295420-1fb5-48c4-b8cb-e6fb3c72503f","name":"Rodil, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-6737-7342","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Shorty","key":"kandjengopau","last":"Kandjengo","name":"Kandjengo, Shorty","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Donovan","key":"maaszpau","last":"Maasz","name":"Maasz, Donovan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Vincenzo","key":"dandreapedh","last":"D'Andrea","name":"D'Andrea, Vincenzo","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Rogerio Abreu","key":"depaulapedh","last":"de Paula","name":"de Paula, Rogerio Abreu","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kasper","key":"rodilpedh","last":"Rodil","name":"Rodil, Kasper","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"David","key":"lamaspedh","last":"Lamas","name":"Lamas, David","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Naska","key":"goagosespedh","last":"Goagoses","name":"Goagoses, Naska","rank":10,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Asnath Paula","key":"kambungapedh","last":"Kambunga","name":"Kambunga, Asnath Paula","rank":11,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel","key":"tanyongwenpedh","last":"Tan Yong Wen","name":"Tan Yong Wen, Daniel","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Chiara","key":"delgaudiopedh","last":"Del Gaudio","name":"Del Gaudio, Chiara","rank":13,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mika Yasuoka","key":"jensenpedh","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Mika Yasuoka","rank":14,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Heike","key":"winschierstheophiluspedh","last":"Winschiers-Theophilus","name":"Winschiers-Theophilus, Heike","rank":15,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tariq","key":"zamanpedh","last":"Zaman","name":"Zaman, Tariq","rank":16,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3661455.3669894","eisbn":["9798400706547"],"pages":"207-210","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 18th Participatory Design Conference","title":"PDC '24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85204902234"],"sdg":["10. Reduced Inequalities","17. Partnerships for the Goals","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-dbfd54b5-466f-4f3c-8768-7a62d27384c7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Comparative Insights for Community-Based Co-design : Bi-directional Inclusive Strategies Between Marginalised Communities and Researchers in Participatory Design","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-736429","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The mental health issues of refugees displaced by violence and affected by humanitarian crises are significant but may be underestimated by healthcare providers. This paper reports on a five-month field trial of a digital screening tool in the Kutupalong refugee camp in Bangladesh. The screening tool is based on the WHO SRQ-20 standard with twenty questions to identify people showing symptoms of mental health issues. The paper demonstrates that not only can digital mental health interventions identify people with symptoms of mental health issues in a refugee camp, but the approach can also identify predictors of mental health issues. First, findings show that of 1630 persons screened, 20.1% exhibited indications of significant mental health issues. Second, a binary logistic regression analysis finds that three of the questions or variables have high ‘odds ratios’ and are, therefore, significant in their ability to predict mental health issues. These predictors are substantiated through semi-structured interviews with the refugees that highlight particular issues of concern.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Ahsan, Hasib","Christensen, Lars Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776401"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital health","Digital mental health interventions","HCI4D","ICT4D","Public health"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"digital mental health in humanitarian crisis in bangladesh","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106869518/Digital_Mental_Health_in_Humanitarian_Crisis_in_Bangladesh.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This study received funding from the Novo Nordisk Foundation[grant numbers 0055633 & 0062495]"],"id":"S01-000.00-776401","identifier":[{"id":"85201014459","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-5a6d3228-5d5d-4e76-9c07-e055d7709304"],"keyword":["Binary logistic regression","Digital Health","Digital mental health interventions","HCI4D","ICT4D","Public health","Rohingya Refugee"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-63F1BF988636F7FACFEDCADBC3EC78CE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/106869518/Digital_Mental_Health_in_Humanitarian_Crisis_in_Bangladesh.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Business Innovation, Information Systems and Digital Innovation","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","locid":"0bdda5a8-b38a-4532-b9a2-e5d9a98c05a7","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","orcid":"0000-0002-7812-2652","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-031-66982-8_20","eisbn":["9783031669828"],"isbn":["9783031669811"],"issn":["18684238"],"pages":"286-302","publisher":"Springer","series":"IFIP Advances in Information and Communication Technology","status":"p","title":"Implications of Information and Digital Technologies for Development","volume":"708"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201014459"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-5a6d3228-5d5d-4e76-9c07-e055d7709304"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Digital Mental Health in Humanitarian Crisis in Bangladesh","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776401","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This paper delves into the emotional landscape of researchers engaged in participatory design and action research. It addresses the less-discussed aspects of unwanted emotions, such as guilt and shame, experienced by researchers during and post-project. The paper explores the guilty dichotomy between the researchers' intent to contribute positively and the reality of unmet expectations. The unease stemming from perceived exploitation and the limitations of project impact is scrutinised, highlighting the tightrope walked in participatory design. Furthermore, the paper discusses the paradox of professional recognition versus the ongoing adversities faced by what may be marginalised communities. Through reflective analysis, this paper contributes to a deeper understanding of the emotional landscape traversed by researchers in participatory design and action research. It underscores the need for supportive frameworks that address these emotional aspects, advocating for ethical reflexivity and sustained engagement strategies that align closely with community needs and well-being.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Christensen, Lars Rune","Ahsan, Hasib"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776417"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Digital mental health interventions","ICT4D action research design research","ICT4D participative development participatory design","Participatory Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the researcher s plight guilt and shame in participatory design and action research","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3661455.3669865","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776417","identifier":[{"id":"85204888908","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7a44eac9-4787-422b-bef1-e5b587e7d83d"],"keyword":["ICT4D, action research, design research","ICT4D, participative development, participatory design","Participatory Design","digital mental health interventions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2BA9A10BF206810F51B44AADA18D7991"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3661455.3669865","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","locid":"0bdda5a8-b38a-4532-b9a2-e5d9a98c05a7","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","orcid":"0000-0002-7812-2652","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3661455.3669865","eisbn":["9798400706547"],"pages":"19-23","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"PDC '24: Proceedings of the Participatory Design Conference 2024: Exploratory Papers and Workshops - Volume 2","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85204888908"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7a44eac9-4787-422b-bef1-e5b587e7d83d"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Researcher's Plight: Guilt and Shame in Participatory Design and Action Research","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776417","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Essential thrombocythemia (ET), polycythemia vera (PV), and primary myelofibrosis (MF) are myeloproliferative neoplasms (MPN). Inflammation is involved in the initiation, progression, and symptomology of the diseases. The gut microbiota impacts the immune system, infection control, and steady-state hematopoiesis.  Methods: We analyzed the gut microbiota of 227 MPN patients and healthy controls (HCs) using next-generation sequencing. We expanded our previous results in PV and ET patients with additional PV, pre-MF, and MF patients which allowed us to compare MPN patients collectively, MPN sub-diagnoses, and MPN mutations (separately and combined) vs. HCs (N = 42) and compare within MPN sub-diagnoses and MPN mutation. Results: MPN patients had a higher observed richness (median, 245 [range, 49–659]) compared with HCs (191.5 [range, 111–300; p =.003]) and a lower relative abundance of taxa within the Firmicutes phylum; for example, Faecalibacterium (6% vs. 14%, p <.001). The microbiota of CALR-positive patients (N = 30) resembled that of HCs more than that of patients with JAK2V617F (N = 177). In JAK2V617F-positive patients, only minor differences in the gut microbiota were observed between MPN sub-diagnoses, illustrating the importance of this mutation.  Conclusion: The gut microbiota in MPN patients differs from HCs and is driven by JAK2V617F, whereas the gut microbiota in CALR patients resembles HCs more.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Eickhardt-Dalbøge, Christina Schjellerup","Nielsen, Henrik V.","Fuursted, Kurt","Stensvold, Christen Rune","Andersen, Lee O.Brien","Lilje, Berit","Larsen, Morten Kranker","Kjær, Lasse","Christensen, Sarah Friis","Knudsen, Trine Alma","Skov, Vibe","Sørensen, Anders Lindholm","Ellervik, Christina","Olsen, Lars Rønn","Christensen, Jens Jørgen Elmer","Nielsen, Xiaohui Chen","Hasselbalch, Hans Carl","Ingham, Anna Cäcilia"],"cuid":["S02-088.16-725067"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"auth