":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Software, Data, People & Society"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"lehigh university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Lehigh University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"new jersey institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"New Jersey Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"university of michigan ann arbor","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Michigan, Ann Arbor","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ingrid","key":"ericksonpau","last":"Erickson","name":"Erickson, Ingrid","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Adriana S.","key":"vivacquapau","last":"Vivacqua","name":"Vivacqua, Adriana S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Naja L.","key":"holtenmøllerpau","last":"Holten Møller","locid":"1373f0c3-8420-4023-874a-25270bf667d6","name":"Møller, Naja Holten","name_org":"Holten Møller, Naja L.","orcid":"0000-0002-4324-3745","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Eric","key":"baumerpau","last":"Baumer","name":"Baumer, Eric","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Yvette","key":"wohnpau","last":"Wohn","name":"Wohn, Yvette","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise","key":"barkhuuspau","last":"Barkhuus","name":"Barkhuus, Louise","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Lionel P.","key":"robertpau","last":"Robert","name":"Robert, Lionel P.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3361110","issn":["25730142"],"issue":"GROUP","journal":"Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction","paperid":"229","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the ACM on Human-Computer Interaction","volume":"3"},"review":"No Review","scoID":["2-s2.0-85076681119","2-s2.0-85077839113"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-df2d409b-2b4c-47c1-80a7-4cec200670d4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Editor's welcome","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-526738","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The lack integration of public organizations and services is a recurring challenge for scholars, policymakers, and citizens. Within the e-government field, scholars have presented web-stage models, which predict that digitization will lead to a fully integrated public sector and seamless user journeys for citizens. Although these models have not delivered on their promises, scholars and policymakers still regard digitization as a means to integrate the public sector, achieve efficiency gains, and improve service quality. We argue that the web-stage models overlook barriers to integration, as they are mostly conceptual, and primarily focus on the potential of technology, rather than its actual implementation and use. Moreover, the models occur on the organizational level of analysis and ignore citizens and their actual experiences. Therefore, we present an empirical study of how citizens experience cross-organizational interaction during benefit application following a family break-up or divorce. Through observations, contextual interviews, focus group discussions and workshops we identify seven challenges citizens experience. These challenges make citizens aware that they are interacting with different organizations and break their experience of an integrated public sector. Further, the challenges cause citizens to turn from the digital channels towards traditional channels to complete their interaction. Thus, the lack of integration challenge both citizens’ satisfaction and efficiency gains from public sector digitalization.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Østergaard Madsen, Christian","Christensen, Lars Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383510"],"event":{"acronym":"IRIS","title":"Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Actual use","Cross organizational interaction","E government","Integration","Seamlessness"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integrated and seamless single parents experiences of cross organizational interaction","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84241239/Madsen_Christensen_2018_Integrated_and_seamless._Single_Parents_Experiences_of_Cross_Organizational_Interaction.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-383510","ids":["itu-989d6a8b-9693-4fd3-94ad-13130c253399"],"keyword":["Actual use","Cross-organizational interaction","E-government","Integration","Seamlessness"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8F9C3DFA8ED8E8F47669FDF2C89BE0B2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84241239/Madsen_Christensen_2018_Integrated_and_seamless._Single_Parents_Experiences_of_Cross_Organizational_Interaction.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Research Centre for Government IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"østergaardmadsenpau","last":"Østergaard Madsen","locid":"74a08deb-18e1-48d0-a86e-ed6675da92ab","name":"Østergaard Madsen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-5984-561X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["18919863"],"issue":"5","publisher":"Scandinavian Chapter of the Association for Information Systems (AIS) - Scandinavian IRIS","series":"IRIS: Selected Papers of the Information Systems Research Seminar in Scandinavia","status":"p","title":"IRIS 2018 Proceedings"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-989d6a8b-9693-4fd3-94ad-13130c253399"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Integrated and seamless? : Single Parents’ Experiences of Cross-Organizational Interaction","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383510","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Accounting for the ways in which ICT initiatives are worked into local communities is part of rendering “the local perspectives” within ICT4D. This paper is part of that. Based on in-depth fieldwork, we investigate the integration of an agricultural information service into a rural community in Bangladesh. We find that it takes work beyond the initial design and cursory introduction of the service to make the service work in a low-income rural community: it takes the strength of the farmers self-help groups to circulate the messages by word-of-mouth, it takes posters placed at key junctions according to a socio-geographic understanding of the village manifest in a map, and it (ideally) involves the support of the elite of the community via the broadcast of messages at places of high symbolic value. It takes all this in addition to a well-made information service delivering relevant and timely messages on for example agricultural matters. Hence, reducing the issue to one of technical delivery mechanism does not tell the full story.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Christensen, Lars Rune","Ahsan, Hasib","Rashid, Mamunur","Das, Badal Kumar"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-701226"],"event":{"acronym":"IFIP 9.4","title":"International Conference on Social Implications of Computers in Developing Countries"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Bangladesh","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Welthungerhilf","mPower Social Enterprises Ltd"],"keyword":["Agricultural Information Services","Bangladesh","ICT4D","Local Perspectives","Rural Community Integration"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a local perspective working an agricultural information service into a rural community","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-19115-3_22","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-701226","identifier":[{"id":"85065709603","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-0841e9ba-6ba4-4c9e-a384-788bf914653a"],"keyword":["Agricultural Information Services","Bangladesh","ICT4D","Local Perspectives","Rural Community Integration"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-56294DA866009A5B3CA923614B1C1B08"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-030-19115-3_22","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"welthungerhilf","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Welthungerhilf","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"bd","key":"mpower social enterprises ltd","loc":["Bangladesh","Asia, South"],"name":"mPower Social Enterprises Ltd","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","locid":"0bdda5a8-b38a-4532-b9a2-e5d9a98c05a7","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","orcid":"0000-0002-7812-2652","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mamunur","key":"rashidpau","last":"Rashid","name":"Rashid, Mamunur","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Badal Kumar","key":"daspau","last":"Das","name":"Das, Badal Kumar","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-030-19115-3_22","isbn":["9783030191146","9783030191153"],"publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Information and Communication Technologies for Development. Strengthening Southern-Driven Cooperation as a Catalyst for ICT4D"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065709603"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0841e9ba-6ba4-4c9e-a384-788bf914653a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Local Perspective: Working an Agricultural Information Service into a Rural Community","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-701226","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"EEG (Electroencephalography) allows to elicit the mental state of the user, which in turn reveals the user emotion, which is an important factor in HMI (Human Machine Interaction). Researchers across the globe are developing new techniques to increase the EEG accuracy by using different signal processing, statistics, and machine learning techniques in this work we will discuss the most common techniques that can yield to better results, along with discussing the common experiment steps to classify the emotion, starting from collecting the signal, and extracting the features and select the best feature to classify the emotions. Along with highlighting some standing problems in field and potential growth areas.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Christensen, Lars Rune","Abdullah, Mohamed Ahmed"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383878"],"event":{"acronym":"CIBCB","title":"IEEE Conference on Computational Intelligence in Bioinformatics and Computational Biology"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Sudan"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Sudan University of Science & Technology"],"keyword":["EEG based emotion recognition","Feature extraction","Human Machine Interaction","Machine Learning in Neuroscience","Signal processing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"eeg emotion detection review","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/CIBCB.2018.8404976","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383878","identifier":[{"id":"85051022091","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-b368588b-9db7-4c41-a08b-20b7a850d2d4"],"keyword":["EEG-based emotion recognition","Feature Extraction","Human-Machine Interaction","Machine Learning in Neuroscience","Signal Processing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E17AD896344549EC335DA9F861A81A95"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/CIBCB.2018.8404976","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sd","key":"sudan university of science technology","loc":["Sudan","Africa"],"name":"Sudan University of Science & Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohamed Ahmed","key":"abdullahpau","last":"Abdullah","name":"Abdullah, Mohamed Ahmed","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/cibcb.2018.8404976","eisbn":["9781538613993"],"isbn":["9781538614006"],"publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2018 IEEE Conference on Computational Intelligence in Bioinformatics and Computational Biology (CIBCB)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85051022091"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-b368588b-9db7-4c41-a08b-20b7a850d2d4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"EEG emotion detection review","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383878","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Despite the advent of a flurry of digital technologies, paper prevails on manufacturing shopfloors. To understand the roles and value of paper on the shopfloor, we have studied the manufacturing practices at two state-of-the-art automotive supplier facilities, applying ethnographic fieldwork, in-depth interviews, as well as photo and document analysis. We find that paper has unique affordances that today's digital technologies cannot easily supplant on current shopfloors. More specifically, we find four paper practices: (1) creating and adapting individual information spaces, (2) reinterpreting information, (3) combining information handover with social interaction, and (4) visual cuing. We discuss these practices and the unique affordances of paper that currently support shopfloor workers and also consider the limitations of paper, which are becoming increasingly apparent, since more tasks increasingly depend on real-time information.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Heinrich, Peter","Richter, Alexander","Christensen, Lars Rune","Schwabe, Gerhard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383071"],"event":{"acronym":"GROUP","end":"2018-01-10","place":"Sanibel Island, us","start":"2018-01-07","title":"ACM INTERNATIONAL CONFERENCE ON SUPPORTING GROUP WORK 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affordances","Digital Artifacts","Manufacturing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"creating reinterpreting combining cuing paper practices on the shopfloor","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82422186/2018_Heinrich_et_al_Group_2018_Paper_on_the_shopfloor_PRINT_final.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383071","identifier":[{"id":"85052127454","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-7adb3b37-0cf7-4a74-960f-4290822dc956"],"keyword":["Affordances","Digital Artifacts","Manufacturing","Paper Practices","Shopfloor"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AC8F93C7945ED67A087B6C8B709F0688"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82422186/2018_Heinrich_et_al_Group_2018_Paper_on_the_shopfloor_PRINT_final.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"heinrichpau","last":"Heinrich","name":"Heinrich, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Alexander","key":"richterpau","last":"Richter","name":"Richter, Alexander","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Gerhard","key":"schwabepau","last":"Schwabe","name":"Schwabe, Gerhard","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3148330.3148341","isbn":["9781450355629"],"pages":"274-283","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"GROUP '18","title":"Proceedings of the 2018 ACM Conference on Supporting Groupwork"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052127454"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-7adb3b37-0cf7-4a74-960f-4290822dc956"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Creating, Reinterpreting, Combining, Cuing: Paper Practices on the Shopfloor","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383071","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we present Krishi Kontho (literally, “agricultural voices”), which is an agricultural information service that utilises pre-recorded voice messages, and SMS, that are pushed to smallholder farmers mobile phones at intervals carefully choreographed with the life cycles of their crops. We present the design of the service, and we present the result of an eleven-month field trial in rural Bangladesh. Findings indicate that this type of service, that synchronises messages with cultivation practice, may improve crop yields while reducing the use of agricultural inputs such as fertiliser and pesticides. We find that the farmers in the field trial deemed the service to be of value to them in regard to improving their agricultural practices. We conclude by discussing our findings and their implications for the design of agricultural information services, including the challenge of designing for specific temporalities, or rhythms of practice, in rural Bangladesh and elsewhere.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Christensen, Lars Rune","Ahsan, Hasib","Akand, Eshrat"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382491"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Agricultural Information Service","Crop Lifecycle Synchronization","Field Trial in Rural Bangladesh","Pre recorded Voice Messages","Smallholder farmers"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"krishi kontho an agricultural information service in bangladesh","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3240167.3240225","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382491","identifier":[{"id":"85056598524","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-51c273d8-fb0a-4236-8067-b7fd317b6846"],"keyword":["Agricultural Information Service","Crop Lifecycle Synchronization","Field Trial in Rural Bangladesh","Pre-recorded Voice Messages","Smallholder Farmers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0B3129D835E500509FE09C00559616DA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83641722/NordiChi_Krishi_Kontho_v35_PURE.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3240167.3240225","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Climate IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, REFLACT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hasib","key":"ahsanpau","last":"Ahsan","locid":"0bdda5a8-b38a-4532-b9a2-e5d9a98c05a7","name":"Ahsan, Hasib","orcid":"0000-0002-7812-2652","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Eshrat","key":"akandpau","last":"Akand","name":"Akand, Eshrat","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3240167.3240225","isbn":["9781450364379"],"pages":"203-214","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '18 Proceedings of the 10th Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056598524"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-51c273d8-fb0a-4236-8067-b7fd317b6846"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Krishi Kontho: An Agricultural Information Service in Bangladesh","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382491","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Prophylaxis for gastrointestinal stress ulceration is frequently given to patients in the intensive care unit (ICU), but its risks and benefits are unclear. METHODS: In this European, multicenter, parallel-group, blinded trial, we randomly assigned adults who had been admitted to the ICU for an acute condition (i.e., an unplanned admission) and who were at risk for gastrointestinal bleeding to receive 40 mg of intravenous pantoprazole (a proton-pump inhibitor) or placebo daily during the ICU stay. The primary outcome was death by 90 days after randomization. RESULTS: A total of 3298 patients were enrolled; 1645 were randomly assigned to the pantoprazole group and 1653 to the placebo group. Data on the primary outcome were available for 3282 patients (99.5%). At 90 days, 510 patients (31.1%) in the pantoprazole group and 499 (30.4%) in the placebo group had died (relative risk, 1.02; 95% confidence interval [CI], 0.91 to 1.13; P=0.76). During the ICU stay, at least one clinically important event (a composite of clinically important gastrointestinal bleeding, pneumonia, Clostridium difficile infection, or myocardial ischemia) had occurred in 21.9% of patients assigned to pantoprazole and 22.6% of those assigned to placebo (relative risk, 0.96; 95% CI, 0.83 to 1.11). In the pantoprazole group, 2.5% of patients had clinically important gastrointestinal bleeding, as compared with 4.2% in the placebo group. The number of patients with infections or serious adverse reactions and the percentage of days alive without life support within 90 days were similar in the two groups. CONCLUSIONS: Among adult patients in the ICU who were at risk for gastrointestinal bleeding, mortality at 90 days and the number of clinically important events were similar in those assigned to pantoprazole and those assigned to placebo. (Funded by Innovation Fund Denmark and others; SUP-ICU ClinicalTrials.gov number, NCT02467621 .).","author_count":138,"contributors":["Krag, Me