ianskovsøndergaardoth","last":"Lundberg","locid":"efa78851-464f-4fde-969e-866a0c56bb6f","name":"Lundberg, Lillian Skov Søndergaard","rank":76,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["30354950"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1056/nejmoa1714919","issn":["00284793","15334406"],"issn_org":["00284793"],"issue":"23","journal":"The New England Journal of Medicine","pages":"2199-2208","status":"p","title":"The New England Journal of Medicine","title_org":"New England Journal of Medicine","volume":"379"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056307726"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f184ed6d-bb0e-4214-9c40-7bfbebc83ef8","au-ec537654-cf6b-4dec-a6d0-a7d8b62ef49f","ku-0119f748-7a43-445d-953f-1a51a98ef938"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pantoprazole in Patients at Risk for Gastrointestinal Bleeding in the ICU","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-094.66-011540","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Prosthetic joint failure is mainly caused by infection, aseptic failure (AF), and mechanical problems. Infection detection has been improved with modified culture methods and molecular diagnostics. However, comparisons between modified and conventional microbiology methods are difficult due to variations in specimen sampling. In this prospective, multidisciplinary study of hip or knee prosthetic failures, we assessed the contributions of different specimen types, extended culture incubations, and 16S rRNA sequencing for diagnosing prosthetic joint infections (PJI). Project specimens included joint fluid (JF), bone biopsy specimens (BB), soft-tissue biopsy specimens (STB), and swabs (SW) from the prosthesis, collected in situ, and sonication fluid collected from prosthetic components (PC). Specimens were cultured for 6 (conventional) or 14 days, and 16S rRNA sequencing was performed at study completion. Of the 156 patients enrolled, 111 underwent 114 surgical revisions (cases) due to indications of either PJI (n = 43) or AF (n = 71). Conventional tissue biopsy cultures confirmed PJI in 28/43 (65%) cases and refuted AF in 3/71 (4%) cases; one case was not evaluable. Based on these results, minor diagnostic adjustments were made. Fourteen-day cultures of JF, STB, and PC specimens confirmed PJI in 39/42 (93%) cases, and 16S rRNA sequencing confirmed PJI in 33/42 (83%) cases. One PJI case was confirmed with 16S rRNA sequencing alone and five with cultures of project specimens alone. These findings indicated that JF, STB, and PC specimen cultures qualified as an optimal diagnostic set. The contribution of sequencing to diagnosis of PJI may depend on patient selection; this hypothesis requires further investigation.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Larsen, Lone Heimann","Khalid, Vesal","Xu, Yijuan","Thomsen, Trine Rolighed","Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","Christensen, Poul Hedevang","Jørgensen, Mogens Brouw","Kappel, Andreas","Laursen, Mogens Berg","Nielsen, Poul Torben","Pedersen, Christian","Rasmussen, Sten","Riis, Jess Tvede","Simonsen, Ole","Aleksyniene, Ramune","Bertelsen, Henrik Christian","Fisker, Rune Vincents","Frost, Majbritt","Kubik, Magdalena","Iyer, Victor Vishwanath","Ørsted, Iben","Nielsen, Kåre Lehmann","Nielsen, Jeppe Lund","Nielsen, Per Halkjær","Petersen, Kristian Kjær","Arendt-Nielsen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-108317"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["The PRIS Study Group"],"keyword":["16S","16S RNA","Biofilm","Biofilms","Diagnostics","Infection","Joint Prosthesis","Joint infections","RNA","Ribosomal"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"differential contributions of specimen types culturing and 000000000016s rrna sequencing in diagnosis of prosthetic joint infections","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/JCM.01351-17","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-108317","identifier":[{"id":"29444832","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000430856400014","type":"wos"},{"id":"85046301622","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-c8c627d1-64c1-42ab-a5ec-155e63c9cd5e"],"keyword":["16S","16S RNA","Biofilm","Biofilms","Diagnosis (microbiology)","Diagnostics","Infection","Joint infections","Joint prosthesis","Prospective clinical study","Prosthesis infections","RNA","Ribosomal"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B9665901A99112E9E26F9153BAF05407"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/286770231/e01351_17.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/JCM.01351-17","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Microbiology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Diagnostik"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"the pris study group","name":"The PRIS Study Group","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lone Heimann","key":"larsenloneheimannpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9f22747b-7a91-42b6-94ea-866d8c78c7e0","name":"Larsen, Lone Heimann","orcid":"0000-0001-5639-4449","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Vesal","key":"khalidvesalpau","last":"Khalid","locid":"c5d6d87f-9cbb-42b4-b20d-26b2a2b89b14","name":"Khalid, Vesal","orcid":"0000-0001-5507-0645","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yijuan","key":"xuyijuanpau","last":"Xu","locid":"8ad5fe79-e9e1-445e-9069-6c1cf9b21b15","name":"Xu, Yijuan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Trine Rolighed","key":"thomsentrinerolighedpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"2a598ca5-d398-4f6f-a07a-e27982669ee8","name":"Thomsen, Trine Rolighed","orcid":"0000-0002-7393-9372","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Carl","key":"schønheyderhenrikcarlpau","last":"Schønheyder","locid":"d35b264a-6efc-467d-ac9d-e558542ef8a8","name":"Schønheyder, Henrik Carl","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corre