{"abstract":"On the basis of an ethnographic field study among artificial life researchers, this article proposes the concept of allusive machines to describe how technical systems variously allude people into shaping their own beliefs. The concept of allusive machines is inspired by previous research on persuasive technology, which defines technologies as instruments with the explicit purpose of changing human attitudes and behaviours, and the notion of theory machines, which refers to how objects in the world stimulate new theoretical formulations. We particularly introduce the concept of allusive machines to the analysis of how robot technology operates allusively to hatch new ideas and knowledge about life, for both designers in the laboratory as well as general publics during demonstrations. Focusing on Alter, an android based on artificial neuronal networks, we show how the concept of allusive machines is useful to rethink the relationship between designers and users analytically by showing how technical systems, like Alter, become allusive to human thinking and acting.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Lindegaard, Jannik Friberg","Christensen, Lars Rune"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382160"],"event":{"acronym":"NordiCHI","title":"Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Allusive Machines","Ethnographic field study","Human Technology Interaction","Persuasive technology","Robot Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"allusive machines encounters with android life","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83641730/Allusive_Machines_v15_PURE.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382160","identifier":[{"id":"85056587987","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-3cac7f6a-afc1-4c9a-a499-4d978d770b45"],"keyword":["Allusive Machines","Ethnographic Field Study","Human-Technology Interaction","Persuasive Technology","Robot Technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BC2E16543D3C959E28EBD59345383483"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83641730/Allusive_Machines_v15_PURE.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jannik Friberg","key":"lindegaardpau","last":"Lindegaard","name":"Lindegaard, Jannik Friberg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3240167.3240189","isbn":["9781450364379"],"pages":"114-124","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of NordiCHI 2018"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85056587987"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-3cac7f6a-afc1-4c9a-a499-4d978d770b45"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Allusive Machines: Encounters with Android Life","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382160","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Ensuring ethical value exchange is moving to the forefront of the global challenges that HCI will have to address in the coming years In this position paper, we argue that applying a context-sensitive, sociotechnical approach to HCI can help meet the challenge. The background is that the life of marginalized people in contemporary society is challenging and uncertain. The marginalized can face health and cognitive issues as well as a lack of stability of social structures such as family, work and social inclusion. Three questions are of concern when innovating together with people ‘at the margins’: how can we describe users without attempting to stereotype badly, what sociotechnical HCI methods fit the local societal context, and how to make the design sustainable in face of current planetary challenges (e.g., climate change)? We adapt the sociotechnical HCI approach called human work interaction design (HWID) to meet the challenges of designing for ethical value exchange. We present three cases of service design, and suggest how to add a fourth similar case using the HWID approach during the INTERACT ‘field trip plus workshop’. We conclude that applying a context sensitive sociotechnical HCI framework implies that both the backend and frontend of service design and product innovations should be executed and valorized from with the local context.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Abdelnour-Nocera, José","Nielsen, Lene","Christensen, Lars Rune","Clemmensen, Torkil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383632"],"event":{"acronym":"INTERACT","title":"IFIP TC.13 International Conference on Human-Computer Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of West London"],"keyword":["Context sensitive design","Ethical value exchange","Human Computer Interaction HCI","Marginalized communities","Service Design","Social inclusion","Sustainable design","human work interaction design HWID","planetary challenges","sociotechnical approach"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"socio technical hci for ethical value exchange a case of service design and innovation at the margins in resource constrained environments","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82305437/INTERACT_2017_Adjunct_FINAL_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383632","ids":["itu-a251092c-fca4-40f5-93b7-0447df5a6dec"],"keyword":["context-sensitive design","ethical value exchange","human work interaction design (HWID)","human-computer interaction (HCI)","marginalized communities","planetary challenges","service design","social inclusion","sociotechnical approach","sustainable design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0B4DE1959FD76B0549F766850ED2F2C2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82305437/INTERACT_2017_Adjunct_FINAL_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of west london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of West London","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"José","key":"abdelnournocerapau","last":"Abdelnour-Nocera","name":"Abdelnour-Nocera, José","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Torkil","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","name":"Clemmensen, Torkil","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788193126097"],"issn":["03029743"],"pages":"254-262","publisher":"Springer","series":"Lecture Notes in Computer Science","status":"p","title":"The 16th IFIP TC13 International Conference on Human–Computer Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a251092c-fca4-40f5-93b7-0447df5a6dec"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Socio-technical HCI for Ethical Value Exchange: A Case of Service Design and Innovation ‘at the Margins’ in Resource Constrained Environments","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383632","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Digital devices play an important role in medical treatment and will in the future play a larger role in connection to cures of health-related issues. Traditionally medicine has been tested by clinical double blind, randomized trials to document the efficacy and safety profile. When it comes to the use of digital devices in treatments the protocols from the field of medicine is adopted. The question is whether or not this evidence based approach is useful when dealing with digital devices and whether the understanding of the efficiency of a treatment can be obtained without also looking at usability and lifestyle issues. Based on a case study of epilepsy, a literature study of protocols for investigating treatments using digital medical devices, the set-up of studies, the design of a current protocol for clinical trials, and finally preliminary results, we discuss if clinical trials have to include usability studies to determine if a treatment is effective.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Lene","Christensen, Lars Rune","Sabers, Anne"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383454"],"event":{"acronym":"OzCHI","title":"Conference of the Australian Computer-Human Interaction"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Clinical trial","Evidence Based Medicine","Lifestyle issues","Medical devise","Usability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"do we have to include hci issues in clinical trials of medical devices a discussion","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82435103/p352_nielsen.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383454","identifier":[{"id":"85044224245","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-94c9f649-64da-4c13-824b-83662c3aec88"],"keyword":["Clinical Trial","Evidence-based medicine","Lifestyle issues","Medical devise","usability"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4D81C3DFF6A30D0D8F14FF904475BD44"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82435103/p352_nielsen.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1052b289-f510-4c5a-9662-2db48c12ebc2","name":"Nielsen, Lene","orcid":"0000-0003-1768-7147","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"saberspau","last":"Sabers","name":"Sabers, Anne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3152771.3156135","eisbn":["9781450353793"],"pages":"352-355","place":"Brisbane","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"November 28-December 1, 2017, Brisbane, QLD, Australia","title":"OzCHI '17, Proceedings of the 29th Australian Conference on Computer-Human Interaction"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044224245"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-94c9f649-64da-4c13-824b-83662c3aec88"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Do we have to Include HCI Issues in Clinical Trials of Medical Devices? : – A Discussion","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383454","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Ensuring ethical value exchange is moving to the forefront of the global challenges that HCI will have to address in the coming years In this position paper, we argue that applying a context-sensitive, sociotechnical approach to HCI can help meet the challenge. The background is that the life of marginalized people in contemporary society is challenging and uncertain. The marginalized can face health and cognitive issues as well as a lack of stability of social structures such as family, work and social inclusion. Three questions are of concern when innovating together with people ‘at the margins’: how can we describe users without attempting to stereotype badly, what sociotechnical HCI methods fit the local societal context, and how to make the design sustainable in face of current planetary challenges (e.g., climate change)? We adapt the sociotechnical HCI approach called human work interaction design (HWID) to meet the challenges of designing for ethical value exchange. We present three cases of service design, and suggest how to add a fourth similar case using the HWID approach during the INTERACT ‘field trip plus workshop’. We conclude that applying a context sensitive sociotechnical HCI framework implies that both the backend and frontend of service design and product innovations should be executed and valorized from with the local context.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Abdelnour-Nocera, José","Nielsen, Lene","Christensen, Lars Rune","Clemmensen, Torkil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-280450"],"event":{"end":"2017-09-29","place":"Mumbai, in","start":"2017-09-25","title":"The 16th IFIP TC13 International Conference on Human–Computer Interaction","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of West London"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-CBS","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"socio technical hci for ethical value exchange a case of service design and innovation at the margins in resource constrained environments","src":["cbs"],"src-code":["DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/82305437/INTERACT_2017_Adjunct_FINAL_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-280450","ids":["cbs-3539ea27-45a9-45ec-a1ec-bb5799cf9a36"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2B05578A9DE5C4D584F721ADCCED6A4C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/portalfiles/portal/82305437/INTERACT_2017_Adjunct_FINAL_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of west london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of West London","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"cbs copenhagen business school","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-CBS","l3nl":"Copenhagen Business School","l3nn":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"CBS Copenhagen Business School","namevar":["Copenhagen Business School, Department of Digitalization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-CBS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"José","key":"abdelnournocerapau","last":"Abdelnour-Nocera","name":"Abdelnour-Nocera, José","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torkil","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","locid":"8f33094c-9f68-4674-ba9c-33a67db0d011","name":"Clemmensen, Torkil","orcid":"0000-0002-0934-2336","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anirudha","key":"joshipedh","last":"Joshi","name":"Joshi, Anirudha","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Devanuj K.","key":"balkrishanpedh","last":"Balkrishan","name":"Balkrishan, Devanuj K.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Girish","key":"dalvipedh","last":"Dalvi","name":"Dalvi, Girish","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Marco","key":"wincklerpedh","last":"Winckler","name":"Winckler, Marco","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788193126097"],"pages":"254-262","place":"Bombay","publisher":"Indian Institute of Technology Bombay","status":"p","subtitle":"Adjunct Proceedings","title":"Human-Computer Interaction - INTERACT 2017"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Copenhagen Business School","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["cbs-3539ea27-45a9-45ec-a1ec-bb5799cf9a36"],"src":["CBS Copenhagen Business School"],"title":"Socio-technical HCI for Ethical Value Exchange : A Case of Service Design and Innovation ‘at the Margins’ in Resource Constrained Environments","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-280450","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Based on ethnographic fieldwork, and the modelling of work processes at a medical department, this paper considers some of the opportunities and challenges involved in working with models in a complex work setting. The paper introduces a flexible modelling tool to CSCW, called the DCR Portal, and considers how it may be used to model complex work settings collaboratively. Further, the paper discusses how models created with the DCR portal may potentially play a key role in making a cooperative work ensemble appreciate, discuss and coordinate key interdependencies inherent to their cooperative work practices.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Christensen, Lars Rune","Hildebrandt, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383602"],"event":{"acronym":"C&T","title":"International Conference on Communities and Technologies"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CSCW","Collaborative Work Practices","DCR Portal","Ethnographic fieldwork","Work Process Modelling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modelling cooperative work at a medical department","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83457483/Christensen_Hildebrandt_2017.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383602","identifier":[{"id":"85025121871","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-a0682094-ae95-4249-ba2b-007adbd9eef4"],"keyword":["CSCW","Collaborative Work Practices","DCR Portal","Ethnographic Fieldwork","Work Process Modelling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3F13D79A2B3B117C140F0D09C29EBF7D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/83457483/Christensen_Hildebrandt_2017.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Rune","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"92f6c3f3-0ad2-40fc-b278-69170f87567d","name":"Christensen, Lars Rune","orcid":"0000-0001-7204-465X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"hildebrandtpau","last":"Hildebrandt","name":"Hildebrandt, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3083671.3083682","isbn":["9781450348546"],"pages":"46-55","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"C&amp;T '17 Proceedings of the 8th International Conference on Communities and Technologies"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85025121871"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a0682094-ae95-4249-ba2b-007adbd9eef4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modelling Cooperative Work at a Medical Department","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383602","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The atomic simulation environment (ASE) is a software package written in the Python programming language with the aim of setting up, steering, and analyzing atomistic simulations. In ASE, tasks are fully scripted in Python. The powerful syntax of Python combined with the NumPy array library make it possible to perform very complex simulation tasks. For example, a sequence of calculations may be performed with the use of a simple 'for-loop' construction. Calculations of energy, forces, stresses and other quantities are performed through interfaces to many external electronic structure codes or force fields using a uniform interface. On top of this calculator interface, ASE provides modules for performing many standard simulation tasks such as structure optimization, molecular dynamics, handling of constraints and performing nudged elastic band calculations.","author_count":37,"contributors":["Hjorth Larsen, Ask","Mortensen, Jens Jorgen","Blomqvist, Jakob","Castelli, Ivano E.","Christensen, Rune","Dulak, Marcin","Friis, Jesper Deleuran","Groves, Michael N.","Hammer, Bjørk","Hargus, Cory","Hermes, Eric D.","Jennings, Paul C.","Jensen, Peter Bjerre","Kermode, James","Kitchin, John R.","Kolsbjerg, Esben Leonhard","Kubal, Joseph","Kaasbjerg, Kristen","Lysgaard, Steen","Maronsson, Jon Bergmann","Maxson, Tristan","Olsen, Thomas","Pastewka, Lars","Peterson, Andrew T","Rostgaard, Carsten","Schiotz, Jakob","Schutt, Ole","Strange, Mikkel","Thygesen, Kristian S.","Vegge, Tejs","Vilhelmsen, Lasse","Walter, Michael","Zeng, Zhenhua","Jacobsen, Karsten W."],"cuid":["S03-094.79-027601"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hjorth Larsen, Ask"],"country":["Germany","Iceland","Norway","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Bro